    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d46">

                <pb facs="0138" n="56" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg56"/>

                <head>Mr. Judd to Mr.
                        Hunter</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 100.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 8, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> On the 6th instant a deputation from the
                    “Berlin Workingmen’s Union,” consisting of Messrs. A. Korig, L. Hoff, R. Krebs,
                    Robert Nouvel, and Lœhmann, presented an address of condolence in relation to
                    the death of Mr. Lincoln.</p>
                <p>That Union is composed of nine hundred members, and is one of the influential
                    clubs of Berlin.</p>
                <p>I thanked them for their kind sympathies, and promised to forward the address to
                    the government of the United States, to be laid before the people. Annexed is a
                    translation into English, made by the secretary, Mr. Kreismann.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>N. B. JUDD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Hunter</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                    <p>(For accompaniment see Appendix, separate volume.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
